{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"The 3-D launch removes per-row division and stays bit-exact; a 1024-element tile wins almost every workload, with a small-shape fallback. Before using another verifier attempt, I’m investigating whether an error-corrected half-width formulation can meet the unusually strict tolerance—this is the only route to a materially larger speedup, and it can be evaluated locally without risking the saved correct candidate."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch\n\ntorch.manual_seed(7);m=256;k=2432;o=256\nx=torch.rand((m,k),device='cuda');w=torch.rand((o,2*k),device='cuda');b=torch.rand(o,device='cuda')\nwl=w[:,:k];wr=w[:,k:]\nref=torch.cat((x,x),1)@w.t()+b\ns=wl+wr\n# Several error-free-transform residual forms\nres1=(wl-s)+wr\nres2=wl+(wr-s)\ns64=(wl.double()+wr.double())\nres64=(s64-s.double()).float()\nvariants={\n 'sum':x@s.t()+b,\n 'sum+res1':x@s.t()+x@res1.t()+b,\n 'sum+res2':x@s.t()+x@res2.t()+b,\n 'sum+res64':x@s.t()+x@res64.t()+b,\n 'split':x@wl.t()+x@wr.t()+b,\n 'double_math':(x.double()@s64.t()+b.double()).float(),\n}\nfor n,y in variants.items():\n d=(y-ref).abs();tol=1.7e-7+1.1920928955078125e-7*ref.abs()\n print(n,'max',d.max().item(),'mean',d.mean().item(),'ratio',(d<=tol).float().mean().item(),'exact',(d==0).float().mean().item())\n# Compare ref against correctly rounded real result in double\nreal=x.double()@s64.t()+b.double();d=(ref.double()-real).abs()\nprint('ref-vs-real','max',d.max().item(),'mean',d.mean().item())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
